      "title": "UNC-Asheville Employment Opportunities | &quot;Temporary Position&quot; - Assistant Director of Campus Recreation (Club Sports)",
      "description": "UNC-Asheville Employment Opportunities | &quot;Temporary Position&quot; - Assistant Director of Campus Recreation (Club Sports) Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Search Position Description Library Search Classifications Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Annual Security and Safety Report/Jeanne Clery Act Notice of Filing for Labor Condition Applications Benefits Summary About Asheville UNC Asheville Human Resources \"Temporary Position\" - Assistant Director of Campus Recreation (Club Sports) Located in the Blue Ridge Mountains in Western North Carolina, UNC Asheville is the designated public liberal arts campus in the University of North Carolina system. UNC Asheville is nationally known for the quality of our student-centered teaching, mentoring of undergraduates in research, interdisciplinary learning, and striving to be an inclusive campus community. UNC Asheville’s commitment to increasing and sustaining the diversity of our faculty, staff, and students is reflected in our strategic plan goals of diversity and inclusion, and social sustainability. Women, traditionally under-represented minorities, and people with disabilities are encouraged to apply. Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Community Expectations During this time it is important that the community understand how UNC Asheville operates and what is expected of community members as we work together to prioritize everyone’s health and safety. Please see UNC Asheville's Community Expectations for more information. UNC Asheville's Community Expectations. Posting Details Position Information Position Title \"Temporary Position\" - Assistant Director of Campus Recreation (Club Sports) Division Student Affairs Department Campus Recreation Position Summary The primary purpose of this position is to develop, plan, recruit, implement, supervise, and evaluate a comprehensive competitive club sport program. The club sports program comprises the competitive and recreational club sports. The incumbent will develop and expand current program offerings; travel and recruit for new members, develop and manage budgets; and implement, supervise, review and administer the club sport activities and operations. The incumbent will also design, develop, and implement a comprehensive training and leadership development program for club sport officers and coaches, to include training topics such as safety, travel, fundraising, insurance and waivers, use of university name and trademarks/logos, budgeting, officer development, hosting competitions, space allocation and reservations. In addition, the incumbent will outreach to Admissions, Student Affairs, Athletics, student organizations and other campus departments to assess student interests, student learning outcomes, and increase participation, retention, and recruitment for UNC Asheville students. Responsibilities and Duties: Clubs Sports Management (50%) ● Oversee all aspects of the UNC Asheville Club Sports Program. ● Develop, design, and implement a comprehensive training and leadership development program for club sport officers, to include updating the current club sport handbook and providing training on topics such as safety, travel, fundraising, insurance and waivers, use of university name and trademarks/ logos, budgeting, officer development, hosting competitions, space allocation and reservations, and other topics related to sport club programs. ● Develop an outreach plan to provide information sessions and encourage the formation of new club sports. ● Oversee all club sport budgets, including allocations, fundraising and expenditures. ● Review and approve all club sport activities such as travel, memberships, participation with National Governing Bodies, club sport uniforms, events, official volunteers, coaches, and payments according to department and university protocols. ● Oversee all club sport equipment acquisition and maintenance, as well as reservation of spaces. ● Some travel may be required for marketing and support at club sport competitions. Club Sport Recruitment (25%) ● Identify opportunities to recruit new sports and members by traveling and representing UNC Asheville. Work with Admissions to navigate best practices and recruitment cycles. ● Identify talent in members and coaches to grow club sports at UNC Asheville. ● Identify conferences and camps hosted each summer at UNC Asheville for potential recruitment. ● Some travel for recruitment to sporting events and with Admissions may be required. Administration/Supervision (25%) ● Develop long term strategic plans for program areas of responsibility. Plans should align with department and university goals and include core values, directions and assessment. ● Conduct regular assessments of program, department, and divisional goals. ● Coordinate and order supplies, equipment, travel, etc. as needed according to university procurement processes and procedures. ● Plan, develop, implement, and assist with Campus Recreation special events, informal recreation, daily operations, and facility functions in collaboration with the other department members. ● Support Campus Recreation and the Division of Student Affairs in student development and University events. This includes but is not limited to move in day(s), graduation(s), family weekend, homecoming and other campus wide initiatives and events. The Assistant Director for Club Sport is the lead administrator for Club Sports. Other duties as assigned. Position Number Full-Time/Part-Time/Intermittent Full-Time (40 hours/week) Salary Information $21 to $23.50 an hour Posting Detail Information Posting Number T0196 Minimum Education/Experience/Skills Bachelor’s degree with significant experience in team management and recruitment. All degrees must be received from appropriately accredited institutions. Preferred Education/Experience/Skills Master’s degree in sport management, sport administration, higher education and administration, physical education, recreational management, or similar field. Experience with experience working with college age populations admission and recruitment, team management, developing student learning outcomes, leadership development, assessment, and applying student development theory. Certifications in CPR /First Aid/ AED and/or professional rescue a plus. Strong computer software knowledge including Excel, EMS , and website updates. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Experience administering a comprehensive club sport program, recruitment, leadership development, budgeting, team management, working with national governing bodies, working knowledge of several sports, as well as knowledge of college aged student identity development theory and application, assessment and evaluation skills, and at least two years of experience programming sport programs. Must possess excellent organization and communication skills, Microsoft office, and knowledge of or ability to learn and utilize computer software programs such as EMS . Work Schedule and Hours This is a Temporary, Full-Time position with an early summer break and opportunity for re-employment contract late summer. The work schedule will be flexible based on the activities for which this person is responsible. There will be frequent evening and weekend hours, as well as travel for recruitment and tournaments. Posting Date 09/22/2025 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Anticipated Start Date Special Instructions to Applicants Community Expectations During this time it is important that the community understand how UNC Asheville operates and what is expected of community members as we work together to prioritize everyone’s health and safety. Please see UNC Asheville’s Community Expectations for more information. UNC Asheville’s Community Expectations. Quicklink for Posting https://uncash-sb.peopleadmin.com/postings/8496 Background/E-Verify Credential Verification University Safety Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Resume Optional Documents Other Documents Equal Opportunity / Affirmative Action Employer UNC Asheville is committed to equality and diversity of experiences for our students, applicants and employees. Qualified individuals are encouraged to apply regardless of socio-economic status, gender expression, gender and sexual identity, culture, and ideological beliefs. UNC Asheville is an Equal Employment Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer and will not discriminate against applicants and employees on the basis of race, ethnicity, national origin, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, disability, political affiliation, protected veteran status, genetic information, and any other legally protected status with respect to all terms, conditions, and privileges of university-sponsored activities, employment, and the use of university facilities. Last refresh: Wednesday March 11, 2026 01:20:59 AM To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
